# The burrow tree PAX carries as /bin/ssh and /bin/burrow-keygen (px104;
# tools/mkburrow builds it, tools/install-burrow installs it).
#
# burrow is an ssh client in wolf (wolffe-lang/burrow, the burrow track):
# OpenSSH-compatible for the profile it speaks (curve25519-sha256,
# ssh-ed25519 host and user keys, chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com, strict
# kex), strict known_hosts checking, publickey login with an unencrypted
# Ed25519 key in OpenSSH's format, one command a session with GIT_PROTOCOL
# by SendEnv: the ssh den's ssh:// and scp-like remotes start. Its clean
# room is the SSH RFCs and OpenSSH's PROTOCOL notes (burrow's README); PAX
# reads no more of its tree than building it needs.
#
# burrow 4ed28a4 (2026-11-09): B5's burrowd (burrow#11) and px112's password
# authentication against /etc/shadow, the head of burrow's px112 PR, pinned
# in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.37 / lupin 0.1.59 / wolf-std
# 2411d868 (std.x.crypto.passwd; the wolf archive bundles 5b3a5994, so
# tools/mkburrow fetches wolf-std at the pin). tools/mkburrow builds it with
# THAT toolchain, through burrow's own tools/build --static, in two
# checkouts, refusing two digests, and installs all three programs:
# /bin/ssh, /bin/burrow-keygen and /bin/burrowd. burrow's merge gauntlet
# printed these digests for that build (its check-static step);
# tools/mkburrow prints whether its build does, and holds the two checkouts
# to each other, not to these (the static binary depends on the libc.a it
# links):
#   (burrow's final gauntlet at 4ed28a4 is running; its three lines follow)
BURROW_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/burrow
BURROW_REV=4ed28a4046b269eb685c17ef311626bc6d4f21e6
